  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rods&amp;Cones project, Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rods&amp;Cones (R&amp;C) was founded in 2019. R&amp;C develops and sells camera and remote image technology for the medical sector, surgery in particular. By means of a portable camera and screen in a spectacle frame, surgical interventions can be shared live via a video connection. This allows others, such as experts or students, to watch the operation from a remote location.In Kenya, R&amp;C wants to demonstrate through a demonstration project that the so-called &#x201c;hub-and-spoke&#x201d; model is of added value in the Kenyan context. This model is based on one hub location (advanced hospital) linked via R&amp;C technology to multiple rural healthcare facilities that have to deal with limited knowledge and possibilities. R&amp;C wants to demonstrate that the technology is locally of added value and provides a higher quality of care by demonstrating various use cases.</narrative>
  </description>
